findings.failure_scenario:
The plan fixes these points:
- fixture-v1 is a stand-in (line 150), and GATE-V1 stores 'stand-in versions and hashes' (line 482);
- rule 1 refuses when a stand-in hash differs from GATE-V1's (line 315);
- the ask step refuses until 'the labels-v1 freeze line' is in FREEZES.md (lines 405-406);
- rule 1 also refuses an ask line that predates the labels freeze (line 316);
- after an insufficient verdict, 'the enlarged held-out set is scored once more, GATE-V1 unchanged' (lines 452-453).
den-label refuses a new labels version until the fixture is frozen again over the same sessions, and the new fixture manifest has a different sha256 even though the old sessions' box files are unchanged. So the rescore hits rule 1 (fixture hash ≠ GATE-V1's) and cannot run without editing GATE-V1. The old held-out sessions' ask lines also predate the labels-v2 freeze. The ask step's labels-v1 pin either refuses the new sessions or lets them be asked before their own labels are frozen. A plausible outcome (straddled bounds with 4 sessions) therefore leaves N2 with no legal way forward.
